    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">TTG201 · Assessment 2/5</span>\n<h2>Group assignment</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13225 · assessment table (verbatim)</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">TTG201 · Đầu điểm 2/5</span>\n<h2>Group assignment</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13225 · bảng đánh giá (nguyên văn)</p></div>\n<div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type / Loại</span><span class=\"v\">on-going</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Weight / Trọng số</span><span class=\"v\">25.0%</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Parts / Số phần</span><span class=\"v\">1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Completion criteria / Điều kiện hoàn thành</span><span class=\"v\">&gt;0</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Duration / Thời lượng</span><span class=\"v\">OP1: Submit on session 29. This is a 5-7 minutes video assignment. OP2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">CLO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO2, CLO3, CLO4, CLO5, CLO6, CLO7, CLO8, CLO9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Question type / Dạng câu hỏi</span><span class=\"v\">OP1: Presentation, written report and video assignment. OP2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Knowledge &amp; skill / Kiến thức &amp; kỹ năng</span><span class=\"v\">OP1: Base on requirements of lecturer<br><br>OP2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Grading guide / Hướng dẫn chấm</span><span class=\"v\">OP1: Class is divided into 4-5 groups.<br><br>The plan of the fieldtrip will be built by class and submitted to teacher for approval before travelling.<br><br>The video is made as a result of the fieldtrip.<br><br>Each group will be required to do a task in the trip and recording the task they implement. The details requirements are as follow:<br><br>1. The video record should show the title: &quot;Field trip for Tourism Geography subject&quot;.<br><br>2. The video should have university's logo and students should wear school's uniform (if possible).<br><br>3. The video should declare the names of group's members.<br><br>4. Each group can record the backstage sceneries for enriching the content of the video.<br><br>5. Topics will be chosen randomly and assign for students by teachers. Topics suggested are:<br><br>- Introduce overview (general) information about the chosen site (i.e. history of establishment, natural/cultural tourism resources, features of the destination's attraction, suitable tourism products).<br><br>- Introduce clearly about tourism infrastructure and superstructure of the site (i.e: accommodation, food and beverage, entertainment and recreational activities, etc.).<br><br>- Introduce about tourism route to travel to the site, means of transportation used to visit the site and the stopover(s) during the route of travelling.<br><br>- Travel tips and note for tourists when visiting the site (time, season, climate, what to bring, how to deal with locals, what to try in the site)<br><br>- Identify problems/issues of the site and give recommendation to improve the situation (from your own thought of the site).<br><br>An additional written report is submitted together with the video that clearly explain what you've done in the video as requested in each group (it will work as the subtitle for the video).<br><br>On the day of the presentation, each group will spend time answering questions from lecturers and other groups about his field trip<br><br>OP2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Note / Ghi chú</span><span class=\"v\">OP1: All assignments should be typed and double-spaced with 12-point font, and must be submitted in soft copy. A deduction of 10% of the assignment mark will be applied for each day of late submission<br><br>Evaluation will be based on presentation, video and written report (recommended 40%, 40%, 20% accordingly)<br><br>OP2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Sessions in the plan that mention it</h3>\n<ul><li>Session 18 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT GUIDELINE</li><li>Session 19 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT GUIDELINE</li><li>Session 57 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li><li>Session 58 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li><li>Session 59 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li><li>Session 60 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Buổi trong kế hoạch có nhắc tới</h3>\n<ul><li>Buổi 18 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT GUIDELINE</li><li>Buổi 19 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT GUIDELINE</li><li>Buổi 57 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li><li>Buổi 58 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li><li>Buổi 59 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li><li>Buổi 60 — GROUP ASSIGNMENT</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">No practice paper for this subject in the Exam Room yet.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">Phòng thi chưa có đề luyện cho môn này.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Exam-strategy notes and worked past papers: coming later.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Chiến lược làm bài và chữa đề: sẽ bổ sung sau.</div></div>"
